<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mie Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mie Prefecture is a prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinai">Kinki region</a> of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ise-bay">Ise Bay</a>, with its capital at Tsu. It was formed in 1876 from the old provinces of Ise, Shima, Iga and part of Kii, after the abolition of the domains in 1871. It contains the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ise-grand-shrine">Ise Grand Shrine</a>, the most sacred shrine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shinto">Shinto</a>, and the industrial city of Yokkaichi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mie-prefecture.jpg" alt="Mie Prefecture" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tawashi2006 · CC BY 2.1 jp · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunrise_of_the_Wedded_Rocks03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
